WEBVTT

00:00.193 --> 00:01.342
- [Voiceover] So we have an equation.

00:01.342 --> 00:05.786
It says, a-x plus three-x
is equal to b-x plus five.

00:05.786 --> 00:09.418
And what I want to do
together is to solve for x,

00:09.418 --> 00:11.047
and if we solve for x it's going to be

00:11.047 --> 00:14.391
in terms of a, b, and other numbers.

00:14.391 --> 00:17.038
So pause the video and
see if you can do that.

00:17.038 --> 00:18.640
All right now, let's do this together,

00:18.640 --> 00:19.260
and what I'm going to do,

00:19.260 --> 00:21.349
is I'm gonna try to
group all of the x-terms,

00:21.349 --> 00:23.353
let's group all the x-terms
on the left-hand side.

00:23.353 --> 00:25.953
So, I already have a-x and
three-x on the left-hand side.

00:25.953 --> 00:29.309
Let's get b-x onto the left-hand
side as well, and I can do

00:29.309 --> 00:34.057
that by subtracting b-x from both sides.

00:34.057 --> 00:37.551
And if I subtract b-x from both sides,

00:37.551 --> 00:41.499
I'm going to get on the right-hand side,

00:41.499 --> 00:44.192
I'm going to have a, or
on the left-hand side,

00:44.192 --> 00:47.984
a-x plus three-x

00:47.984 --> 00:52.701
minus b-x, so I can do
that in that color for fun,

00:52.701 --> 00:56.996
minus b-x, and that's
going to be equal to...

00:56.996 --> 00:59.155
Well, b-x minus b-x is just zero,

00:59.155 --> 01:00.211
and I have five.

01:00.211 --> 01:02.255
It is equal to five.

01:02.255 --> 01:04.251
And now what I can do is,

01:04.251 --> 01:07.015
I can factor an x out
of this left-hand side

01:07.015 --> 01:09.116
of this equation, out of all of the terms.

01:09.116 --> 01:12.796
So, I can rewrite this as x times...

01:12.796 --> 01:15.792
Well, a-x divided by x is a.

01:15.792 --> 01:18.589
Three-x divided by x is three,

01:18.589 --> 01:20.585
and then negative b-x divided by x

01:20.585 --> 01:23.847
is just going to be negative b.

01:23.847 --> 01:26.545
I could keep writing
it in that pink color.

01:26.545 --> 01:28.862
And that's all going to be equal to five.

01:28.862 --> 01:30.709
And now, to solve for x I can just divide

01:30.709 --> 01:35.166
both sides by, the thing that
x is being multiplied by,

01:35.166 --> 01:37.329
by a plus three minus b.

01:37.329 --> 01:40.013
So, I can divide both sides by

01:40.013 --> 01:44.237
a plus three minus b.

01:44.237 --> 01:47.175
A plus three minus b.

01:47.175 --> 01:49.415
On this side, they cancel out.

01:49.415 --> 01:52.515
And, I have x is equal to five

01:52.515 --> 01:56.598
over a plus three

01:56.598 --> 01:59.747
minus b, and we are done.

01:59.747 --> 02:02.394
Let's do one more of these.

02:02.394 --> 02:03.729
So, another equation here.

02:03.729 --> 02:04.936
We have a...

02:04.936 --> 02:09.487
Here we have a times the
quantity, five minus x,

02:09.487 --> 02:11.496
is equal to b-x minus eight.

02:11.496 --> 02:12.796
So, once again, pause the video

02:12.796 --> 02:16.020
and see if you can solve for x.

02:16.020 --> 02:17.428
Well, the way I like to approach these

02:17.428 --> 02:20.028
is let's just expand everything all out.

02:20.028 --> 02:21.386
So, let me just distribute this a,

02:21.386 --> 02:23.454
and then I'm gonna collect
all the x-terms on one side,

02:23.454 --> 02:25.670
and all of the non-x-terms
on the other side,

02:25.670 --> 02:28.526
and essentially do what I
just did in the last example.

02:28.526 --> 02:31.068
So, let's first distribute this a.

02:31.068 --> 02:33.343
So the left-hand side becomes

02:33.343 --> 02:36.571
five-a, I could say a
times five or five-a,

02:36.571 --> 02:40.567
minus a-x, a-x,

02:40.567 --> 02:43.269
that is going to be equal to

02:43.269 --> 02:45.743
b-x minus eight.

02:45.743 --> 02:48.854
Now we can subtract b-x from both sides.

02:48.854 --> 02:51.303
So, we're gonna subtract
b-x from the left-hand side,

02:51.303 --> 02:52.812
b-x from the right-hand side.

02:52.812 --> 02:53.950
And, once again, the whole
reason I'm doing that,

02:53.950 --> 02:55.702
I want all the x-terms on the left,

02:55.702 --> 02:58.082
and all the non-x-terms on the right.

02:58.082 --> 03:01.530
And, actually, since I want all
the non-x-terms on the right,

03:01.530 --> 03:04.894
I can actually subtract five-a
from both sides, as well.

03:04.894 --> 03:06.634
So I'm kind of doing
two steps at once, here,

03:06.634 --> 03:07.621
but hopefully it makes sense.

03:07.621 --> 03:09.483
I'm trying to get rid of the b-x here,

03:09.483 --> 03:11.247
and I'm trying to get
rid of the five-a here.

03:11.247 --> 03:13.290
So, I subtract five-a there,

03:13.290 --> 03:15.809
and I'll subtract five-a there,

03:15.809 --> 03:19.164
and then let's see what this give us.

03:19.164 --> 03:21.207
So, the five-a's cancel out.

03:21.207 --> 03:22.264
And, on the left-hand side,

03:22.264 --> 03:24.539
I have negative a-x,

03:24.539 --> 03:26.769
negative a-x,

03:26.769 --> 03:28.659
minus b-x,

03:29.510 --> 03:33.269
minus, you know, in that same green color,

03:33.269 --> 03:35.104
minus b-x.

03:35.104 --> 03:37.148
And on the right-hand side,

03:37.148 --> 03:37.982
I have...

03:37.982 --> 03:38.888
This is going to be equal to,

03:38.888 --> 03:40.420
the b-x's cancel out,

03:40.420 --> 03:44.359
and I have negative eight minus five-a.

03:44.359 --> 03:47.304
Negative eight minus,

03:47.304 --> 03:49.707
in that same magenta color,

03:49.707 --> 03:52.586
minus five-a.

03:52.586 --> 03:55.977
And let's see, I have all my x's

03:55.977 --> 03:58.484
on one side, all my
non-x's on the other side.

03:58.484 --> 04:01.386
And here I can factor out an x,

04:01.386 --> 04:04.555
and if I factor out an x, what do I have?

04:04.555 --> 04:05.681
And, actually, one thing
that might be nice.

04:05.681 --> 04:08.317
Let me just multiply both
sides by negative one.

04:08.317 --> 04:10.139
If I multiple both sides by negative one,

04:10.139 --> 04:13.785
I get a-x plus b-x,

04:13.785 --> 04:17.941
plus b-x is equal to

04:17.941 --> 04:20.274
eight plus five-a.

04:20.274 --> 04:22.945
That just gets rid of all
of those negative signs.

04:22.945 --> 04:25.800
And now I can factor out an x here.

04:25.800 --> 04:28.795
So let me factor out an x,

04:28.795 --> 04:30.967
and I get x times

04:30.967 --> 04:34.847
a plus b.

04:34.847 --> 04:39.220
A plus b is going to

04:39.220 --> 04:43.563
be equal to eight plus five-a.

04:43.563 --> 04:45.118
Eight plus five-a.

04:45.118 --> 04:46.691
And we're in the home stretch now.

04:46.691 --> 04:50.902
We can just divide both sides by a plus b.

04:50.902 --> 04:54.962
So we could divide both sides by a plus b.

04:54.962 --> 04:56.958
A plus b.

04:56.958 --> 04:57.934
And we're going to be left with,

04:57.934 --> 05:00.241
x is equal to

05:01.161 --> 05:03.738
eight plus five-a,

05:03.738 --> 05:07.486
plus five-a, over...

05:09.276 --> 05:12.294
Actually, I'll write a and
b in our original colors.

05:12.294 --> 05:16.709
A plus, so this was that a, that a,

05:16.709 --> 05:18.459
plus b.

05:18.459 --> 05:22.556
So this is the b, that's a and b,

05:22.556 --> 05:24.375
a plus b, and we're done.

05:24.375 --> 05:25.738
We have now solved for x

05:25.738 --> 05:30.579
in terms of a's and b's and other things.

05:30.579 --> 05:33.196
And we are all done.
